From b10b12f2e9a3fc8bc2ca34ebaf94f4383b2a40bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:53:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] device: pulse vendor.xrz.check_commit on touch and button
 activity

The XRZ composer counts large updates toward the per-app clean frequency
only while vendor.xrz.check_commit is 1, so a clean frequency never fired
on this GSI. As in the stock PowerManagerService, set it to 1 on touch or
button user activity and back to 0 800 ms after the last such activity.
The property is written only on transitions, on the power manager
thread, and only when ro.bigme.force_client_composition is true.

Change-Id: Ib1e57571966e5e7f557f501ad013cd12d2db7a89

A failing property set is logged once, not on every input burst.
---
 .../server/power/HiBreakXrzCheckCommit.java   | 93 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../server/power/PowerManagerService.java     |  6 ++
 2 files changed, 99 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 services/core/java/com/android/server/power/HiBreakXrzCheckCommit.java

